item.description:
arXiv:2610.36885v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: Let $Z_F(t):=F(1/2+it) H(1/2+it)^{-1/2}$ denote Hardy's function, where the function $F(s)$ belongs to the Selberg class with polynomial Euler product and satisfies the functional equation $F(s)=H(s)\overline{F}(1-\bar{s})$. We prove that for every function of degree $1$ and for certain functions of degree $2$ belonging to the Selberg class, one has
  \begin{align*}
  \max_{T\leq t\leq 2T} \pm Z_F(t) &\gg \exp\left(C_F \sqrt{ \frac{{\log T}}{{\log \log T}} } \right),
  \end{align*}
  where the constant $C_F$ depends on $F(s)$ and are explicitly determined.
